  /// have to supply a country code for the rule to evaluate. In this case,
  /// you configure the rule to only count matching requests, but it will
  /// still generate logging and count metrics for any matches. You can reduce
  /// the logging and metrics that the rule produces by specifying a country
  /// that's unlikely to be a source of traffic to your site.
