  /// Notation (JSON) Pointer . For example, for the JSON payload { "form": {
  /// "primaryphoneline1": "THE_PHONE1", "primaryphoneline2": "THE_PHONE2",
  /// "primaryphoneline3": "THE_PHONE3" } } , the phone number field
  /// identifiers are /form/primaryphoneline1 , /form/primaryphoneline2 , and
  /// /form/primaryphoneline3 . For form encoded payload types, use the HTML
  /// form names. For example, for an HTML form with input elements named
  /// primaryphoneline1 , primaryphoneline2 , and primaryphoneline3 , the
  /// phone number field identifiers are primaryphoneline1 , primaryphoneline2
